<title>SRI LANKA: NTT SAYS PAID FAIR PRICE FOR S.LANKA TELEC.</title>
<headline>NTT SAYS PAID FAIR PRICE FOR S.LANKA TELEC.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Nippon Telephone and Telegraphic Corp (NTT) said on Thursday it had paid a fair price of $225 million for its 35 percent stake in Sri Lanka Telecom (SLT).</p>
<p>&quot;The price is a fair price. NTT feels that there is huge potential in this country. It could become a financial hub of Asia,&quot; Hideaki Kamitsuma, the new chief executive of SLT told a news conference.</p>
</text>
